# Provider-agnostic LLM routing engine

This proof of concept exposes a FastAPI chat API that classifies each request into one of four task groups and executes a configuration-driven provider fallback chain. Routers classify; they never select concrete models.

## Current topology

- Routers: Google `gemini-3.8-flash` → NVIDIA `z-ai/glm-5-3-flash`
- General: G1 Google → G2 OpenRouter → G3 Groq → G4 NVIDIA
- Coding/reasoning: C1 Groq → C2 NVIDIA → C3 OpenRouter → C4 OpenRouter
- Creative: W1 OpenRouter → W2 Google
- Multimodal: M1 NVIDIA → M2 OpenRouter

The exact 12 task-model IDs and metadata are in `.env.example`. The selected free tiers/endpoints are suitable for evaluation, not guaranteed production capacity; provider quotas and catalogs can change.

## Request flow

```text
FastAPI request
→ optional V2 governance eligibility/ranking
→ Google task-group classifier
→ NVIDIA classifier on failure
→ registry candidates for the selected group
→ backend circuit check and one attempt per candidate
→ response gateway
→ response and optional developer diagnostics
```

The task groups are exactly `general`, `coding_reasoning`, `creative`, and `multimodal`. The deterministic legacy default router no longer exists.

## Quick start

```bash
copy .env.example .env
uv sync
uv run uvicorn api.main:app --reload
```

Populate all four provider keys in the private `.env`. `OPENROOUTER_API_KEY` remains a deprecated compatibility alias for the correctly spelled OpenRouter key. `MAX_RETRIES` means maximum explicit conversation-level retries; provider adapters do not retry task calls.

Run tests:

```bash
uv run pytest -q
```

Unit/integration tests use fakes and do not consume cloud quota. The cloud test remains opt-in through `RUN_CLOUD_INTEGRATION=1` and valid credentials.

## Text and image input

Text-only V1/V2 requests remain unchanged. An optional single JPEG, PNG, or WebP image may be supplied as validated base64:

```json
{
  "conversation_id": "example",
  "message": "Describe this image",
  "image": {
    "media_type": "image/png",
    "data_base64": "..."
  }
}
```

Image URLs, audio, video, and image generation are out of scope. Image data is forwarded only at the provider transport boundary and is not retained in conversation state, diagnostics, dashboard history, or exports.

## Resilience and observability

Google, NVIDIA, OpenRouter, and Groq each have one process-local circuit shared by router and task-model calls. Three qualifying backend-transient failures open a circuit for 30 seconds; one half-open probe determines recovery. Health polling only reads circuit snapshots and never changes state. Circuit state resets when the process restarts.

Set `X-Developer-Mode: true` to receive safe task-group, router-attempt, provider-fallback, latency, error-classification, and circuit diagnostics. Normal chat responses do not expose routing internals. Credentials, endpoints, upstream bodies, and image data are never included.

The Streamlit/Plotly evaluation dashboard remains an API-only client:

```bash
uv run streamlit run dashboard/app.py
```

See [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md) for architecture, contracts, testing, and limitations.
